a.c('round_decision','Total Consensus round decision','A positive-budget policy declares convergence, disagreement, escalation and foldback rules. Complete admitted reviewer findings and the exact admitted response precede exactly one closed_done, recurse_next_round or escalate_fh outcome.',[g(0,111,134)])
a.q('round_outcome_partition',['round_decision'],'The total relation over exact policy/source round/vector/response maps refusal-bearing complete vector to closed_done/contract_failure; exact agreement to closed_done/unanimous_agreement; material disagreement with budget to recurse_next_round plus one response-bearing successor basis; disagreement without budget or admitted escalation rule to escalate_fh plus one same-Run hold and provisional unresolved_disagreement. Exhaustion cannot accept or create another round. Only decision_row, draft_ticket, split_ticket, deferment and rejected_finding rulings may be constructed from admitted occurrences/response; no other outcome, classification, ruling, successor or hold is lawful.',[g(0,105,134)])
a.c('consensus_final_result','Consensus final result','Binds subject, panel, policy, rounds, findings, rulings, consensus/dissent classification, terminal outcome, evidence/lineage and result/replay refs; unanimous agreement, partial agreement with dissent, unresolved disagreement and contract failure remain distinct.',[g(0,136,145)])
a.q('single_result_and_fh',['consensus_final_result','round_decision'],'One admitted Run exposes at most one final result. escalate_fh is provisional hold basis: the same Run finalizes to partial agreement for accept_with_dissent or unresolved disagreement for reject. These two choices form the closed consensus-fh-decision vocabulary, never an accepted boolean.',[g(0,69,71),g(0,136,145)])
a.r('response_precedes_successor','required_before','submitter_response','round_decision','The exact source-round submitter response must be ABG-admitted before any successor can be constructed, bound, opened or executed.',[g(1,149,160)],governing=True)
a.q('consensus_graph_execution',['consensus_contract_family'],'GTL declares higher-order reviewer fan-out, explicit attributed vector boundary, canonical submitter F_P over that vector, ordinary ABG result/judgment admission, declared reduction, bounded recursion/foldback. Prompts, selection, merge policy, control and classification remain declarations/contracts. HoG selects inside an admitted program through One Surface; ABG admits GraphCall/frame/C-call/worker/results/events/replay/continuation/retry/F_H. The function is published by, not equal to, that program, cannot bypass evaluateNext and adds no scheduler, writer, wake, retry or closure authority.',[g(1,149,169)])
a.q('consensus_judgment_partition',['round_decision','reviewer_occurrence','submitter_response'],'Deterministic admission owns schemas, digests, attribution, membership, budget, exact agreement and envelopes; reduction uses panel ordinal/profile rather than completion order. F_P owns findings, disputed semantic judgment and attributed response; ABG admits each and binds source-round causality. Unresolved judgment routes F_H. F_D cannot manufacture semantic agreement; F_P cannot waive failed deterministic envelopes.',[g(1,171,179)])
a.q('next_round_refusal',['submitter_response','round_decision'],'Product validation and ABG admission refuse missing response; wrong actor/profile/configuration; another invocation or nonexact source round; forged identity/digest/evidence; or no complete admitted findings-vector binding before any next-round state/task/GraphCall/Frame/C-call. Refusals remain typed non-close truth, append no next-round fact and keep source-round evidence replayable.',[g(1,181,189)])
a.q('ticket_consensus_data_boundary',['consensus_final_result'],'ticket.consensus is ordinary typed result bound to ticket ref/digest; rulings never own status. Consensus cannot change/write/split tickets, invoke triage automatically or admit its ruling as governance truth. Caller/F_H may carry a ruling through ordinary TICKET_METHOD triage and mutation.',[g(0,105,109),g(1,191,195)])
a.c('consensus_workspace','Consensus workspace application','One public workspace contract applies to existing, independently bound alternate and caller-created temporary roots. Temporary roots still require admitted workspace, stable authority basis, immutable binding, catalog, event/result/replay/proof identities; observations create snapshots without changing authority/binding.',[g(2,199,206)])
a.l('consensus_workspace_latitude',['consensus_workspace'],['Use any of the three explicit workspace applications of one contract.','Later contracts may require reviewer isolation or distinct output workspace after declaring ordinary input/output binding authority.'],['Infer per-reviewer isolation, separate output workspace or three runtime modes from these applications.'],[g(2,199,211)])
a.q('consensus_public_path',['consensus_contract_family','consensus_final_result'],'CLI starts canonical Consensus through run.invoke start, supervised One Surface Program start and until=converged; project.read supplies results/replay. Escalation opens a hold in that Run; interaction.respond admits exact actor/capability/hold/provisional result and one accept_with_dissent|reject; run.continue resumes same Run, admits exactly one final result and closes ordinarily. No direct support call, feature CLI verb, new operation or host orchestration. catalog.view may narrow to function/dependencies but cannot widen authority.',[g(2,213,225)])
a.q('consensus_human_topology_affirmation',['consensus_contract_family'],'S05 closure requires direct human affirmation of sole One Surface entry, same-Run causal ABG hold/continuation and absence of rival selection/result/continuation/closure authority. Implementation, tests, review or delegated acceptance cannot supply it implicitly.',[g(2,227,233)])
a.q('consensus_qualification_evidence',['consensus_contract_family'],'The supplied qualification wording requires packed/installed exact 5.0 candidate invocation of published Consensus over one real ticket, at least two distinct reviewer profiles and one exact submitter through admitted program/run.invoke; project.read result/replay; all three workspace applications; no source imports or shell panel/submitter/One Surface control. Controlled agreement, response-gated recurse, and exhausted/unresolved escalation fixtures are required, including round-two negatives for missing/wrong/forged/unbound responses and typed non-close malformed subjects/profiles/findings/responses/rulings/policies/outcomes. Release completeness requires executable GTL validation, installed row, addressable schemas/vocabularies, all fixtures/workspaces, attribution/causality/result/replay. Declaration-only, imperative, legacy-operation or parallel-adapter paths fail; unresolved fixture retains exact Run, consumes one hold once and emits one final result before closure.',[g(3,237,267)],uncertainty='The qualification subsection says 5.0; the enclosing release applicability declaration is not supplied in this chunk and must be reconciled before applying this gate.')
